%% RIBAT — Node Movement / Event Archaeology
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant L as Lender / Operator
  participant UI as Console UI
  participant LOC as Local canonicaliser
  participant BL as Blind boundary
  participant GW as Gateway / Auth
  participant RI as Registry index
  participant REG as Atomic registry
  participant HCS as Hedera topic
  participant MI as Mirror indexer
  participant VER as Verify public
  participant GP as Guardian pool
  participant PAY as Bank settlement

  Note over L,VER: N0 — raw receivable candidate. Raw document, parties, amount and tax IDs remain in lender custody.
  L->>UI: 1. Enter invoice or traite fields
  UI->>LOC: 2. Validate type, jurisdiction and required fields
  LOC->>LOC: 3. Normalise references, dates, parties and amount
  LOC->>LOC: 4. Derive INV1, INV2 and INV3 candidates
  Note over LOC: N1/N2/N3 — three local key nodes. They are comparable fingerprints, not public data.
  LOC->>BL: 5. Blind or hash key candidates
  BL->>GW: 6. Send Q = blinded candidates + member proof
  Note over BL,GW: Privacy boundary: production registry receives no raw invoice, name, amount or portfolio.
  GW->>RI: 7. Authenticated collision query
  RI->>RI: 8. Compare exact key commitments and reissue signals
  alt No matching commitment
    RI-->>GW: 9A. CLEAR
    GW-->>UI: 10A. Clear result + candidate receipt
    UI->>REG: 11A. Atomic register request
    REG->>REG: 12A. Compare-and-set on canonical commitment
    REG->>REG: 13A. Create C1 with rank=1 and consensus timestamp
    Note over REG: C1 — active senior claim node. Contains nullifier, pseudonymous partyId, docHash and status.
    REG->>HCS: 14A. Publish REGISTERED event envelope
    HCS-->>REG: 15A. Consensus timestamp + sequence number
    HCS->>MI: 16A. Mirror event
    MI->>MI: 17A. Update searchable history and epoch accumulator
    MI-->>VER: 18A. Expose redacted proof fields
    VER-->>L: 19A. Verify: status, rank, timestamp, root, simulated/live anchor label
    L->>PAY: 20A. Fund through normal bank rails
  else Matching commitment
    RI-->>GW: 9B. COLLISION + senior rank/timestamp
    GW-->>UI: 10B. BLOCKED, without senior lender identity
    UI->>L: 11B. Stop funding or request mediated review
    Note over UI,L: C2 — later candidate node is not given active priority.
    alt False positive
      L->>GP: 12B. Submit mediated disclosure request
      GP-->>L: 13B. Legitimate twin or confirmed conflict
    else Confirmed conflict
      L->>UI: 12C. Create dispute / freeze proposal
    end
  end

  Note over L,VER: N4 — public event node contains only minimal proof: event type, nullifier, partyId, rank, status and timestamp.
  opt Claim is challenged
    L->>GP: 21. Propose freeze order O with reason and expiry
    GP->>GP: 22. Verify proposer and claim reference
    GP-->>REG: 23. Guardian 1 approval
    GP-->>REG: 24. Guardian 2 approval
    GP-->>REG: 25. Guardian 3 pending / reject / approve
    alt Quorum not reached
      REG-->>GP: 26A. Keep order pending
      REG->>HCS: 27A. Publish ORDER event
    else Quorum reached
      REG->>REG: 26B. Start time-lock
      REG->>HCS: 27B. Publish TIME_LOCK event
      REG->>REG: 28B. Execute after delay
      REG->>REG: 29B. C1 status ACTIVE → FROZEN
      REG->>HCS: 30B. Publish EXECUTED event
      HCS->>MI: 31B. Mirror status transition
      MI-->>VER: 32B. Verify shows FROZEN + order proof
      alt Order renewed through valid process
        GP->>REG: 33B. Renew before expiry
      else No renewal
        REG->>REG: 33C. Auto-expire order
        REG->>REG: 34C. FROZEN → EXPIRED or RELEASED per policy
        REG->>HCS: 35C. Publish EXPIRED event
      end
    end
  end

  opt Receivable is paid or discharged
    PAY-->>L: 36. Settlement confirmation
    L->>REG: 37. Release claim request
    REG->>REG: 38. ACTIVE or FROZEN → RELEASED according to policy
    REG->>HCS: 39. Publish RELEASED event
    HCS->>MI: 40. Mirror final lifecycle status
    MI-->>VER: 41. Verify shows RELEASED and complete history
  end

  Note over MI,VER: N5 — epoch root is periodically published so historical event order can be independently checked.
  MI->>HCS: 42. Publish epoch root / Merkle root
  HCS-->>MI: 43. Root consensus timestamp
  MI-->>VER: 44. Attach root and mirror evidence
